            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kazoo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is what I have to say about this recipe. I wept with joy at the first bite. Do you know how hard it is to eat and cry at the same time? Yet, I pressed on. After that, I wept with sorrow, because there would be a last bite. Knowing that I would soon finish the succulent tri-tip steak that I had left in the marinade for a full day because I forgot I was going to cook it left me in a pool of tears... it was even harder to chew as I sobbed and sobbed... but I managed, oh yes. I managed. After a few minutes, I awoke from my bittersweet bliss, wiped away my tears and resolved myself to make this recipe... again and again. Oh joy! One thing to mention, though, is that I didn't have worchestershire sauce in the house, so I opted to use a certain brand steak sauce in its place (begins with an \"A\")as the flavor of that reminds me of the original ingredient. I'll be making this with the W sauce this week. I'll bet it's even tastier... Thanks for inventing it, YOU ROCK!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "geome"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Should leave out the oil as it prevents the tenderizing effect of the vinegar, oil meat just before grilling, otherwise perfect marinade.",
            "datePublished": "2009-05-29T07:49:36.910Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "krickett"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was excellent but after reading the review from the previous person I used balsamic vinegrette instead of the vinegar. It didn't overpower the other ingredients and made an excellent marinade. I will never buy marinade again!",
            "datePublished": "2009-05-24T18:10:58.593Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LMEasterling"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I usually double all ingredients except for the olive oil, marinate for 1-4 hours (depending on how far ahead I've planned! lol) and then, while the steaks are cooking, boil the leftover marinade with about 1 tsp. cornstarch to make a delicious sauce to put on top of the grilled meat! Mmmm.",
            "datePublished": "2012-02-07T09:11:37.213Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GrittyTray1278"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a very good recipe but like other have said, double the recipe EXCEPT for the olive oil, then add cornstarch to the left over marinade and boil. I use this thickened sauce on top of grilled baked potatoes, or drizzle some on a grilled ear of corn on the cob. HUGE hit in my house and at get togethers!",
            "datePublished": "2022-11-12T15:40:36.304Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Suzy Grinstead"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe should instruct you to add the oil last. Drizzle it in as you whip the other ingredients. This will blend everything together well for a better flavor. I did it this way and my steaks were delicious! (I also decreased the basalmic vinegar by a Tablespoon.)",
            "datePublished": "2020-08-27T23:04:34.300Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jordon"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was awesome! added little fresh rosemary, parsley, and thyme. Then let it marinate for 6 hours. pat dry, remove any sprigs, and grill!",
            "datePublished": "2022-11-22T05:52:11.237Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kathy Williams Diaz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Super great recipe! Only a couple suggestions, anytime I see a recipe with both soy sauce and salt - one's got to go! I totally eliminated the salt, but this still seemed salty to me. I will definitely make again but will reduce soy sauce to 1 T and 3 tsp. This is equal to one third of the original 1/4 C called for in recipe. Also, being I was going to grill this steak I felt with all the oil in this marinade (I knew it would flame up) I should rinse the marinade off the steak before grilling. Glad I did.",
            "datePublished": "2024-07-12T21:59:39.971Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SpeedyMilk2962"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This marinade slaps! I used some red wine as well and used fish sauce instead of the soy and Worcestershire, and it turned out amazing! I actually only marinaded it for 10 minutes or so and then used the leftover marinade to make a sauce. It was really fantastic, everyone said they were the best steak tips they'd ever had! My mom even said, \"This is what I want when I order steak tips\"! Thanks for the recipe! Highly recommend!!",
            "datePublished": "2023-06-04T19:24:53.840Z"
          },
